# Standalone Dropdown Project Template

## Quick Setup Instructions

1. **Create a new React project:**
```bash
npx create-react-app dropdown-project
cd dropdown-project
```

2. **Install Tailwind CSS:**
```bash
npm install -D tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer
npx tailwindcss init -p
```

3. **Configure Tailwind (tailwind.config.js):**
```javascript
module.exports = {
  content: [
    "./src/**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}",
  ],
  theme: {
    extend: {},
  },
  plugins: [],
}
```

4. **Add Tailwind to CSS (src/index.css):**
```css
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;
```

5. **Copy the MultiSelectDropdown files:**
   - Copy `MultiSelectDropdown.jsx` to `src/components/`
   - Copy `MultiSelectDropdown.css` to `src/components/`

6. **Use in your App.js:**
```jsx
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import MultiSelectDropdown from './components/MultiSelectDropdown';
import './App.css';

function App() {
  const [selectedItems, setSelectedItems] = useState([]);

  // Generate test data
  const testOptions = Array.from({ length: 50 }, (_, index) => ({
    id: index + 1,
    name: `Option ${index + 1} - Test Item with Long Name`,
    category: `Category ${Math.floor(index / 10) + 1}`
  }));

  const handleChange = (newSelectedIds) => {
    setSelectedItems(newSelectedIds);
    console.log('Selected:', newSelectedIds);
  };

  return (
    <div className="App p-8 max-w-md mx-auto">
      <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Dropdown Test</h1>
      
      <MultiSelectDropdown
        label="Select Options"
        options={testOptions}
        selectedValues={selectedItems}
        onChange={handleChange}
        displayKey="name"
        valueKey="id"
        searchKeys={["name", "category"]}
        placeholder="Choose options..."
        searchPlaceholder="Search options..."
        className="rounded-lg"
        required
      />

      <div className="mt-6 p-4 bg-gray-100 rounded">
        <h3 className="font-semibold">Selected Items:</h3>
        <p>{selectedItems.length} items selected</p>
        {selectedItems.length > 0 && (
          <ul className="mt-2 text-sm">
            {selectedItems.map(id => {
              const item = testOptions.find(o => o.id === id);
              return <li key={id}>• {item?.name}</li>;
            })}
          </ul>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

7. **Run the project:**
```bash
npm start
```

## File Structure
```
dropdown-project/
├── src/
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── MultiSelectDropdown.jsx
│   │   └── MultiSelectDropdown.css
│   ├── App.js
│   ├── index.css
│   └── index.js
├── package.json
└── tailwind.config.js
```

This will give you a working dropdown with 50 test items to verify the scrolling functionality!